{title: Lay you down}
{artist: Conway Twitty}
{key: G}
{comment: Imported from CountryTabs — verify key and arrangement}
{comment: Source: http://www.countrytabs.com/tablature/Conway_Twitty/Id_Just_Love_To_Lay_You_Down__Chord_37701/}
{comment: Structure: V I C}

{start_of_verse}
I'D Just Love To Lay You Down
Conway Twitty
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_intro}
[G]
There's a lot of ways of sayin', what I want to say to you.
[D] [C] [G]
There's songs and poems and promises and dreams that might come true,
But I won't talk of starry skies or moonlight on the ground,
[D] [C] [G]
I'll come right out and tell ya, I'd just love to lay you down.
{end_of_intro}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]
Lay you down and softly whisper pretty love words in your ear,
[D] [C] [G]
Lay ya down and tell ya all the things a woman loves to hear,
I'll let you know how much it means just havin' you around,
[D] [G]
Oh Darlin' how I'd love to lay ya down.
[G]
There's so many ways your sweet love's made this house into a home,
[D] [C] [G]
You've got a way of doin' little things that turn me on.
Like standin' in the kitchen, in your faded cotton gown,
[D] [C] [G]
With your hair all up in curlers, I'd still love to lay you down.
REPEAT CHORUS)
[G]
When a whole lot of Decembers are showin' in your face,
[D] [C] [G]
Your auburn hair has faded and silver takes it's place,
You'll be just a lovely, and I'll still be around,
[D] [C] [G]
And if I can I know that I'll still love to lay you down.
(Repeat Chorus)
(Change Keys, Down 2 steps to "C")
[F]
Lay you down and softly whisper pretty love words in your ear,
[C] [A#] [F]
Lay ya down and tell ya all the things my woman loves to hear,
I'll let you know how much it means just havin' you around,
[C] [F]
Oh Darlin' how I'd love to lay ya down.
(Change Keys, Down 2 steps to "Bb")
[D#]
Lay you down and softly whisper pretty love words in your ear,
[A#] [G#] [D#]
Lay ya down and tell ya all the things my woman loves to hear,
I'll let you know how much it means just havin' you around,
